## Why This Is Asked

This question probes data governance, access control, and incident response fundamentals for beginner CISSP candidates, with a realistic data-import scenario.

## Key Concepts

- Data classification and handling
- RBAC/ABAC and just-in-time access
- Data provenance and SBOM concepts
- Encryption at rest and in transit; KMS/key rotation
- Immutable audit logging and incident response/testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Validate payload schema and attach a signed attestation
function validateAndSign(payload, signer) {
  // simple schema check
  if (!payload || !payload.data) throw new Error('Invalid');
  const attestation = signer.sign(JSON.stringify(payload));
  return { payload, attestation };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test end-to-end import validation in CI/CD?
- How should failed attestations be handled and remediated?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical zero-trust for admin access, mirroring real enterprise risk of credential theft and lateral movement in hybrid environments.

## Key Concepts
- Zero-trust, device posture, MFA, PIM, Just-In-Time
- Jump hosts, session recording, RBAC, break-glass, SIEM/audit

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-policy: grant only if posture true and MFA passed
if (device.posture && user.mfa && time.inWindow) {
  grantAccess();
} else {
  denyAccess();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure effectiveness (MTTR, number of break-glass events)?
- How would this adapt to cloud-native IAM vs PAM solutions across AWS/Azure?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical CISSP application to real-world, multi-region auth flows, highlighting threat modeling, token lifecycle, and IR readiness.

## Key Concepts
- STRIDE/PASTA for auth/session threats
- JWT, PKCE, JWKS, token rotation, revocation
- mTLS, RBAC/ABAC in a multi-region service mesh
- IR playbooks and testing strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
// Token validation sketch
function validateToken(token, jwks) {
  const payload = decode(token);
  if (payload.iss !== expectedIssuer) return false;
  if (payload.exp < Date.now()/1000) return false;
  // signature verify against jwks...
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate revocation in a scalable way?
- What metrics indicate token compromise?
